Vita: Link's own heaps are three times the original's size, not twenty.

daAlink_c::setOriginalHeap creates Link's archive heap (0xA2800 bytes in the original) and his
shield's (0x7000) inside the game heap. Dusklight multiplies both by twenty "to prevent mods
from crashing with higher-quality models": 13.3 MiB and 573 KiB. On this port the game heap is
27 MiB and there are no mods (patches 0004, 0005), so every creation of Link (a stage change, a
restart after a fall) needs one free block of 13.3 MiB, half the heap. When the largest block is
smaller the allocation fails, and a failed JKRExpHeap allocation stops the game here.

The whole-game sweep hit it twice (Vita3K, 13 Nov): leaving the Forest Temple for Faron Woods
and falling (the restart creates Link again), and leaving the Cave of Ordeals for the desert.
The first reproduces every time with the same numbers: the game heap had 24 MiB free of 27 in
blocks of 13.2 and 9.1 MiB, and the request was 0xCB20A0 bytes (0xA2800 * 20 + the heap's own
header); the call chain is daAlink_c's create -> setOriginalHeap -> JKRExpHeap::create.

What the archive really takes, measured with a receipt (platform/vita/runtime/scene_probe.cpp,
link_heaps): 744 KiB in Ordon clothes, 723 in the hero's clothes, 715 in the Zora armour, 798
as a wolf; the shield's heap 23 KiB. The original's own sizes (650 and 28 KiB) are therefore a
little short on this port, whose structures are larger. Three times the original gives 2.0 MiB
and 86 KiB: 2.5 times the largest use measured, and 11.8 MiB of the game heap back for
everything else. Nothing changes outside TARGET_VITA.

--- a/src/d/actor/d_a_alink_swindow.inc
+++ b/src/d/actor/d_a_alink_swindow.inc
@@ -40,7 +40,15 @@
         u32 var_r29 = 0x90;
         u32 var_r28 = 0x10;
         u32 size = ROUND(i_size, 16);
-#if TARGET_PC
+#if TARGET_VITA
+        // Vita (patches/dusklight/0077): three times the original's size, not twenty. Twenty made
+        // Link's archive heap 13.3 MiB, taken in one piece from the 27 MiB game heap each time
+        // Link is created; when no free block was that large the game stopped (JKRExpHeap's
+        // CRASH on a failed allocation). There are no mods on this port. Measured in Vita3K: the
+        // archive takes 715 to 800 KiB (Ordon clothes, hero's clothes, Zora armour, wolf), the
+        // shield's 23 KiB; three times the original is 2.0 MiB and 86 KiB.
+        size *= 3;
+#elif TARGET_PC
         size *= 20; // Increase Link's heap size to prevent mods from crashing with higher-quality models.
 #endif
         JKRHeap* parent = mDoExt_getGameHeap();
